WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:14.020
Wassup y'all? Today on Thug Notes we bringin
it back to da South Side with Go Set a Watchman

00:00:14.020 --> 00:00:15.520
by Harper Lee.

00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:22.759
Now if you an OG Mockingbird fan, you prolly
'spectin this book to be written from the

00:00:22.759 --> 00:00:27.710
perspective of Scout, or "Jean Louise" as
she called these days. But it ain't like dat,

00:00:27.710 --> 00:00:32.310
girl: In this book, we gettin da lowdown from
a third person omniscient narrator.

00:00:32.310 --> 00:00:37.859
Anyway, it's sometime in the 1950s and 26
year old Jean Louise Finch dun peaced outta

00:00:37.859 --> 00:00:42.840
da boonies of Alabama and now she keepin it
street up in New York. But girl ain't forgotten

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:47.480
her roots, so she hop on a train and swang
back home to Maycomb County to chill wit her

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:52.320
daddy Atticus, whose ol' crusty ass all jacked
up with rheumatoid arthritis now.

00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:57.640
Up at da station, Jean get scooped up by Henry
Clinton, a back when friend of Jean and lawyer

00:00:57.640 --> 00:01:02.140
who work fo' Atticus. This dude don't want
nuthin' mo than to make Jean his biddy fo'

00:01:02.140 --> 00:01:06.780
life. Homeboy might not be no swanky uptown
playa like they do up in New York, but he

00:01:06.780 --> 00:01:10.930
got solid rep up in Maycomb and his love fo'
Jean is legit.

00:01:10.930 --> 00:01:17.100
So Jean drop in at da old crib where Atticus's
sister Alexandra also livin' since SOMEBODY

00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:22.100
gotta wipe Atticus's ass. Atticus all like
"Girl. You hear bout what goin down with this

00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:27.590
whole segregation talk up in the supreme court?"
Jean like "Sho' nuff, pops. Brown vs. Board

00:01:27.590 --> 00:01:30.079
of Education is my jam."

00:01:30.079 --> 00:01:35.030
Round this time, we hera bout how Jean's lil
bro Jem died years ago. And cuz o dat, da

00:01:35.030 --> 00:01:40.600
finch's black cook Calpurnia got all to' up,
chunked deuce, and ain't nobody seen her since.

00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:46.060
Later, errybody gettin' they church on when
they meet up with Uncle Jack Finch, Atticus's

00:01:46.060 --> 00:01:51.549
brutha from the same mutha. Afta' all dat
holy rolling, Jean peep game at a pamphlet

00:01:51.549 --> 00:01:56.789
in Atticus's living room called "The Black
Plague." And this sh** is exactly as racist

00:01:56.789 --> 00:02:02.520
as it sound. Jean like "Alexandra! Da hell
dis mess doin up in mah daddy's house?" Alex

00:02:02.520 --> 00:02:07.289
like "Why you trippin girl? That's some truth
right there. Blacks people ain't sh** compared

00:02:07.289 --> 00:02:11.390
to white people." OH. NO. SHE. DIDN'T.

00:02:11.390 --> 00:02:16.420
Alexandra say da pamphlet came from somethin'
called the Citizen's Council. Since they meetin'

00:02:16.420 --> 00:02:19.910
now,
Jean head to the courthouse where sho' nuff,

00:02:19.910 --> 00:02:25.480
Atticus, Henry and all da Maycomb big dawgs
sitttin round a long table talk bout how blacks

00:02:25.480 --> 00:02:31.170
ain't nuthin' but cockroaches. Atticus. You
were my man, and now you practically attending

00:02:31.170 --> 00:02:34.110
Klan meetings? ET TU, BRUH?

00:02:34.110 --> 00:02:41.909
Jean so to' up by what she see, she throw
up, book it home, and pass da fu** out.

00:02:41.909 --> 00:02:47.550
Jean wake up Monday and get word that Calpurnia's
grandson accidentally wrecked someone's sh**

00:02:47.550 --> 00:02:53.250
wit his hoopty, and now Atticus gonna take
the case just so the NAACP don't get involved.

00:02:53.250 --> 00:02:58.879
Jean go see Calpurnia to show a girl some
love, but Cal don't want nuthin to do wit

00:02:58.879 --> 00:03:05.519
a racist-ass Finch. When Jean like "Cal whatcha
doin to me? Calpurnia ll "Girl, what y'all

00:03:05.519 --> 00:03:08.620
doin to US?" Jean feelin' lonesome as hell.

00:03:08.620 --> 00:03:13.569
So she hit up her uncle Jack and be all like
"Yo. Da hell has my daddy been smokin? How

00:03:13.569 --> 00:03:18.690
da hell did he become a racist all da sudden?"
Girl don't get no straight answer, so she

00:03:18.690 --> 00:03:23.540
roll over to Atticus's office fo' some real
talk. Cept, da only bruh there is Henry, and

00:03:23.540 --> 00:03:27.890
she lay it on him raw sayin she ain't neva'
gonna marry a lil racist bitch.

00:03:27.890 --> 00:03:33.280
When Atticus drop in, Jean like "Pops! Da
fu** you think you doin' wit dat council?"

00:03:33.280 --> 00:03:38.519
Atticus like "Look girl. This ain't no front.
I think da blacks ain't as legit as da whites.

00:03:38.519 --> 00:03:43.140
Straight up." Jean just bout loses her sh**
and tells him dat she ain't never gonna forgive

00:03:43.140 --> 00:03:47.840
him. I mean, she used to look up to Atticus.
Hell. We all did.

00:03:47.840 --> 00:03:52.370
So she book it back home and start packin
her sh** to go back to New York. Uncle Jack

00:03:52.370 --> 00:03:57.920
drop in and give her five across the face
to calm her ass down. Afta' girl spits out

00:03:57.920 --> 00:04:03.239
some blood, Jack po's up some henny and explains
what's goin down. He tell her dat she spent

00:04:03.239 --> 00:04:08.920
her whole life worshipping Atticus like a
god, but truth is, he was bound to disappoint

00:04:08.920 --> 00:04:13.360
her sooner or later. So she gotta sack up
and become her own person.

00:04:13.360 --> 00:04:18.400
Afta dat, Jean bout to driv Atticus home from
work when pops say: "look girl. Even though

00:04:18.400 --> 00:04:22.910
you said some messed up sh** to me, I'm proud
of you. You stood up fo what you think is

00:04:22.910 --> 00:04:29.210
right, and that's how a real G rolls." JEan
like "Ah hell, pops. I love you even though

00:04:29.210 --> 00:04:33.560
you a racist piece of sh**." THE END.

00:04:33.560 --> 00:04:42.280
Now if you ain't already know, there's a lotta
smack talk goin bout how shady this book's

00:04:42.280 --> 00:04:46.500
publication was. But is it all bullsh**? Let's
take a look:

00:04:46.500 --> 00:04:52.880
Fact number 1: Harper Lee is old as sh**.
Girl lives in an assisted living home, and

00:04:52.880 --> 00:04:58.530
has been fo a while. Afta' a stroke in 2007
leavin her sight and ability to hear all jacked

00:04:58.530 --> 00:05:03.570
up, she ain't exactly at the top of her game.
Of course, that don't mean she can't make

00:05:03.570 --> 00:05:07.000
her own decisions, but it sho as hell don't
make it easier.

00:05:07.000 --> 00:05:12.780
Way back in 2002, Harper's lawyer Alice, who
was also her sistah, said Harper would pretty

00:05:12.780 --> 00:05:19.800
much sign any ol pap you slang in front of
her. But when sis died in 2014, legal control

00:05:19.800 --> 00:05:24.490
went to Tonja, a junior partner in Alice's
firm, and SHE da one who started hustlin'

00:05:24.490 --> 00:05:30.710
da manuscript. Most importantly, Harper Lee
spent da last couple DECADES sayin she neva'

00:05:30.710 --> 00:05:32.670
wanted the book to see the light of day.

00:05:32.670 --> 00:05:38.080
But what even IS this thing? Is it a legit
sequel? Well that's definitely what some folk

00:05:38.080 --> 00:05:44.130
thought; but truth is, this sh** was written
BEFORE To Kill a Mockingbird. See, Harper's

00:05:44.130 --> 00:05:51.270
editor read dis manuscript back in 1957, told
Lee it sucked, and made her rewrite it til

00:05:51.270 --> 00:05:56.750
1960, when To Kill a Mockingbird hit the shelves.
So THAT'S why some of Watchman sound EXACTLY

00:05:56.750 --> 00:05:57.730
like the original.

00:05:57.730 --> 00:06:02.730
I mean, peep this, son. These paragraphs are
almost THE EXACT SAME THING.

00:06:02.730 --> 00:06:08.490
So we most likely lookin at is an early draft
of Mockingbird that was chopped n' screwed

00:06:08.490 --> 00:06:12.210
so dat somebody can get in on dat sweet sequel
money

00:06:12.210 --> 00:06:17.550
Anyway, back to the book. When Jean Louise
get back home, girl cain't stop buggin' bout

00:06:17.550 --> 00:06:22.130
how different errything be:
"My aunt is a hostile stranger, my Calpurnia

00:06:22.130 --> 00:06:27.050
won't have anything to do with me, Hank is
insane, and Atticus – something's wrong

00:06:27.050 --> 00:06:32.390
with me, it's something about me. It has to
be because all these people cannot have changed."

00:06:32.390 --> 00:06:32.880
(167)

00:06:32.880 --> 00:06:38.400
Jean Louise recognize dat if she thinkin bout
marrying Henry's crazy racist ass, she gonna

00:06:38.400 --> 00:06:43.370
have to change HERSELF to make it work
'Is that what loving your man is...[y]ou mean

00:06:43.370 --> 00:06:48.500
losing your own identity, don't you?' 'In
a way, yes,' said Henry." (227)

00:06:48.500 --> 00:06:53.950
Man, fu** DAT. Eventually, girl drops dat
scrub sayin she gotta keep it 100 erry day

00:06:53.950 --> 00:06:55.880
and stay true to what she know is right.

00:06:55.880 --> 00:07:01.500
And dat's what da title all about. Like Uncle
Jack say, "Every man's island, Jean Louise,

00:07:01.500 --> 00:07:03.750
every man's watchman, is his conscience."
(265)

00:07:03.750 --> 00:07:08.830
Going to set a watchman basically mean stickin'
to yo guns and defining what you think is

00:07:08.830 --> 00:07:15.410
right and what you think is wrong. Look, as
time go by, things and people gonna change.

00:07:15.410 --> 00:07:19.430
And when they do, you gotta make sho' you
don't just go with the flow. You gotta be

00:07:19.430 --> 00:07:23.240
willing to roll solo to defend what you know
is right.

00:07:23.240 --> 00:07:27.570
And there ain't no change harder fo' my girl
than accepting dat her daddy Atticus ain't

00:07:27.570 --> 00:07:31.890
perfect. Like Jean say:
"But a man who has lived by truth – and

00:07:31.890 --> 00:07:36.450
you have believed in what he has lived – he
does not leave you merely wary when he fails

00:07:36.450 --> 00:07:38.260
you, he leaves you with nothing." (179)

00:07:38.260 --> 00:07:42.730
She spent her whole life lookin' up to this
cat, and now since he sippin on dat haterade

00:07:42.730 --> 00:07:47.690
actin' all racist and sh**, she gotta keep
it real, and make it damn clear that she ain't

00:07:47.690 --> 00:07:50.750
bout dat. But like I said, it's gonna be a
bitch.

00:07:50.750 --> 00:07:55.570
Dat's why all throughout this book da words
"Childe Roland" poppin' up, which allude to

00:07:55.570 --> 00:08:00.760
a dope poem by Robert Browning called "Childe
Roland to the dark Tower Came" where a dude

00:08:00.760 --> 00:08:05.690
gotta beast through a journey to a dark tower
without any of his boys to get his back, and

00:08:05.690 --> 00:08:11.650
when he gets there, he prolly dies. Likewise,
Jean also gotta go on a solo quest- hence

00:08:11.650 --> 00:08:15.840
why she feelin all alone- AND she gotta kill
part of herself to succeed.

00:08:15.840 --> 00:08:20.250
Now even though we don't know what happen
to Childe Roland when he make it to the dark

00:08:20.250 --> 00:08:25.620
tower, we sho know what happen to Jean-Louise
- Uncle Jack tell her she more of a biggot

00:08:25.620 --> 00:08:27.150
than Atticus? Da hell?!

00:08:27.150 --> 00:08:33.320
He say Jean-Louise doin her daddy straight
dirty by focusing on ONE flaw. Just cuz Atticus

00:08:33.320 --> 00:08:38.090
is racist don't mean he ain't a baller in
a million other ways. She used to think Atticus

00:08:38.090 --> 00:08:42.840
was a God. Now she know he just another flawed
flesh n' blood homie.

00:08:42.840 --> 00:08:48.720
Now here's da craziest part- we in the same
position as Jean. Hear me out, playa: To Kill

00:08:48.720 --> 00:08:54.510
a Mockingbird is one of da dopest novels of
all time- the movie is pretty damn legit too.

00:08:54.510 --> 00:09:00.620
And da biggest reason fo' dat is Atticus Finch-
a straight up WARRIOR fo' equality and justice.

00:09:00.620 --> 00:09:04.610
Atticus made GOD knows how many kids wanna
become lawyers.

00:09:04.610 --> 00:09:10.270
So when racist Atticus came hot off the presses
in Go Set a Watchman, some peeps started losin

00:09:10.270 --> 00:09:16.630
their damn minds, sayin Atticus was ruined,
and Harper Lee's legacy was dead. Thing is,

00:09:16.630 --> 00:09:21.520
that's exactly the kinda thing Uncle Jack
tells Jean-Louise at da end of the novel:

00:09:21.520 --> 00:09:26.080
even if someone got a whackass worldview,
you should still give em a chance.

00:09:26.080 --> 00:09:30.770
So is Uncle Jack right? Does Atticus deserve
a chance? Can people who straight up support

00:09:30.770 --> 00:09:36.680
racism, sexism, and homophobia still be good
people? Or does sh** like dat make a brutha

00:09:36.680 --> 00:09:42.240
automatically a monster? I know what I think,
playa... but I ain't gonna set yo watchman

00:09:42.240 --> 00:09:42.720
for ya.

